ealth of the region in new and innovative ways. Minimum Qualifications Board-certified in Internal Medicine or Hospital Medicine Must hold or be eligible for an Ohio medical license and DEA certification Experience managing high-acuity patients in a fast-paced environment A passion for faculty work, including teaching, quality improvement, and innovation Strong teamwork, communication skills, and a commitment to fostering diversity and inclusion within healthcare Preferred Qualifications Essential Functions and percent of time: Wright State University’s Boonshoft School of Medicine ( WSU BSOM ) and Premier Physician Network are seeking dynamic and motivated Hospitalist Faculty to join the Hospital Medicine Division within the Department of Medicine. This is a unique faculty position that offers the opportunity to work with medical students and internal medicine residents at a leading-edge health system recognized nationally for its excellence across numerous specialties. Position Highlights: Faculty Appointment at the Assistant Professor rank (or higher, based on qualifications) Ample opportunities to teach and mentor internal medicine residents, medical students, and other learners across our affiliated programs Benefit from mentorship and a supportive environment fostering growth in clinical care, education, research, quality improvement, and administrative leadership Essential Functions and percent of time (cont'd): Non-Essential Functions and percent of time: Working Conditions This position is a Premier Physician Network position. Please apply at: https://www.premierhealth.com/healthcare-professionals/careers/physician-jobs/opportunities/job-posting/internal-medicine-faculty-hospitalist Special Instructions to Applicants This position is a Premier Physician Network position. Please apply at: https://www.premierhealth.com/healthcare-professionals/careers/physician-jobs/opportunities/job-posting/internal-medicine-faculty-hospitalist Posting Date 10/14/2025 First 