      "title": "Orthopedic Hand Surgeon - Premier Physician Network",
      "description": "WSU - Applicant Portal | Orthopedic Hand Surgeon - Premier Physician Network Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Orthopedic Hand Surgeon - Premier Physician Network Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is a Premier Physician Network position. Please apply at: https://www.premierhealth.com/healthcare-professionals/careers/physician-jobs/opportunities/job-posting/orthopedic-hand-surgeon---employed Position Information Position Information (Default Section) EEO Statement Premier Health and Wright State University are equal employment opportunity employers. Faculty Rank or Job Title Orthopedic Hand Surgeon - Premier Physician Network Job Category: Faculty/Instructional Department School of Medicine Admin EEO number: 27PN016 Position FTE 100% Minimum Annual Salary Eclass 14 Faculty FT Fiscal MO Salary Band: Job Summary/Basic Function: This position is a Premier Physician Network position. Wright State University and Premier Physician Network have entered into an enhanced affiliation agreement that will transform health care delivery in the Miami Valley and beyond. As part of this transformative collaboration, Wright State’s Boonshoft School of Medicine and Premier Physician Network are seeking physicians with a demonstrated ability to enhance and elevate academic health organizations in their mission of clinical care, research, and education. Together, we seek dynamic individuals with a comprehensive understanding of our mission of developing and overseeing innovative health care delivery models, sustaining excellence in clinical care, supporting academic endeavors and promoting and advancing research initiatives and scholarly activity. Outstanding strategic communication and diplomacy skills are critical as Wright State and Premier Physician Network continue to transform the health of the region in new and innovative ways. Minimum Qualifications Board Certified/Board Eligible American Trained, US Citizen or Permanent Resident Status Preferred Qualifications Essential Functions and percent of time: Premier Physician Network and Wright State University’s Boonshoft School of Medicine are seeking Orthopedic Hand Surgeons to join our Integrated Hand Team. Surgeons will be working between our Level I Trauma Center and one of the north or south hospital campuses. Orthopedic Hand Surgeon interested in both complicated hand cases and minimally invasive hand procedures Team oriented physician to grow market share and hand program Call at Level I Trauma Center Competitive compensation, (Two Year Income Guarantee- Year Three Productivity Based Salary based on wRVUs) Paid medical malpractice, robust benefit package, and generous CME allowance Signing bonus, loan forgiveness and relocation will be considered Essential Functions and percent of time (cont'd): Non-Essential Functions and percent of time: Working Conditions This position is a Premier Physician Network position. Please apply at: https://www.premierhealth.com/healthcare-professionals/careers/physician-jobs/opportunities/job-posting/orthopedic-hand-surgeon—-employed Special Instructions to Applicants This position is a Premier Physician Network position. Please apply at: https://www.premierhealth.com/healthcare-professionals/careers/physician-jobs/opportunities/job-posting/orthopedic-hand-surgeon—-employed Posting Date 10/23/2026 First Consideration Date: Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Home 3640 Colonel Glenn Hwy., Dayton, OH 45435 USA To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
